{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The value of this element."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/value"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/value","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"value","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV5valueSSvp","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding/value":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The value of this element."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/value","kind":"symbol","title":"value","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/value","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding":{"title":"MXLEnding","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","abstract":[{"text":"The ending type represents multiple (e.g. first and second) endings. Typically, the start type is associated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"downward jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"typical for second endings that do not conclude a piece. The length of the jog can be specified using the end-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length attribute. The text-x and text-y attributes are offsets that specify where the baseline of the start of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ending text appears, relative to the start of the ending line.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}]}}}